            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:

-  Receptacles

-  All exterior doors

- Header joist

- Storage space behind gable wall in the master bedroom

During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.

</airSeal>
                <HeatingSystem>Have you already thought about having a heat pump? This type of heating system can use up to 3 times less energy than a typical baseboard and needs electricity to operate. However, this kind of system can?????????t operate on temperature below -25 degrees Celsius, it then will require a secondary system to maintain the heat. Which can be provided by the existing heating system. You might be eligible to participate in the Heat Pumps pilot project, please follow the link below for more information;

https://yukon.ca/en/news/expanded-rebates-renewable-home-heating-now-available



</HeatingSystem>
                <AdditionalComments>ETS PROGRAM

For more information concerning the Electrical Thermal Storage Unit, please follow the link below:

http://yukonconservation.org/programs/energy/electric-thermal-storage#:~:text=Electric%20thermal%20storage%20(ETS)%20is,providing%20heat%20throughout%20the%20day 

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
